The original Canvas rendering adapter is MIT licensed with Corporate Brain.
Electron and Chromium retain their own licences and notices.

The ffmpeg-static 5.3.0 downloader package is GPL-3.0-or-later:
https://github.com/eugeneware/ffmpeg-static/tree/v5.3.0
FFmpeg is a separate executable invoked through pipes, not linked into the
employee client. Its applicable licence depends on the downloaded build.
The upstream macOS arm64 build reports --enable-gpl, --enable-version3 and
--enable-nonfree. It is installed for internal server use only; that binary
is NOT redistributable and MUST NOT be added to source, client installers,
server update archives, or GitHub Release assets. Administrators may supply
a separately licensed compatible build using BRAIN_RENDER_FFMPEG.
No FFmpeg executable or its runtime libraries are included in our releases.
Obtain upstream build notices and corresponding sources from:
https://github.com/eugeneware/ffmpeg-static/releases/tag/b6.1.1
https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

Remotion is not installed, imported, executed, or distributed. Its adapter
interface is reserved for future use after the required company licence is
obtained. There is no Remotion subscription or rendering service charge in
this implementation. Configured language-model providers may charge for
code generation under the company's existing API plan.
